<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Panehesy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 1080 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century-bce">11th century BCE</a> · Also known as Pinehesy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Panehesy was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroy-of-india">viceroy</a> of Kush under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ramesses-xi">Ramesses XI</a>, the last king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/twentieth-dynasty-of-egypt">Twentieth Dynasty</a>. Around 1080 BCE he intervened in Thebes with Nubian troops and came into conflict with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/high-priest-of-amun">High Priest of Amun</a>, Amenhotep. Driven back south, he seems to have held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lower-nubia">Lower Nubia</a> independently, and after his struggle Egypt lost effective control of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nubia">Nubia</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/panehesy.jpg" alt="Panehesy" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kairoinfo4u: Mutnedjmet · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Panehesy%E2%80%99s_EA.6_tomb_(Kairoinfo4u).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
